      "steps": [
        {
          "narration": "The walk reads the text one character at a time. If it is an opening bracket, depth gains one and the walk continues.",
          "focus": [
            "scan",
            "scan->openQ",
            "openQ",
            "openQ->deeper",
            "deeper",
            "deeper->scan"
          ],
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-1-step-0.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 6.6,
          "startFrame": 16,
          "frames": 198
        },
        {
          "narration": "A closing bracket takes one off depth. If depth goes negative, a closer arrived with nothing open and the answer is false right away. Any other character simply keeps the walk going.",
          "focus": [
            "openQ->closeQ",
            "closeQ",
            "closeQ->less",
            "less",
            "less->neg",
            "neg",
            "neg->fail",
            "neg->scan",
            "closeQ->scan"
          ],
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-1-step-1.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 10.44,
          "startFrame": 220,
          "frames": 314
        },
        {
          "narration": "When the text runs out, one question remains: did depth come back to exactly zero? Zero means balanced, anything else means brackets were left open.",
          "focus": [
            "scan->fin",
            "fin",
            "fin->ok",
            "ok",
            "fin->fail",
            "fail"
          ],
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-1-step-2.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 9.56,
          "startFrame": 540,
          "frames": 287
        }
      ],
      "durationInFrames": 845
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "The whole trick, ten lines",
      "lang": "python",
      "code": "def is_balanced(text):\n    depth = 0\n    for ch in text:\n        if ch == '(':\n            depth += 1\n        elif ch == ')':\n            depth -= 1\n            if depth < 0:\n                return False\n    return depth == 0",
      "steps": [
        {
          "narration": "The function holds a single number: how deeply nested inside brackets the scan currently is.",
          "lines": [
            1,
            2
          ],
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-2-step-0.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 5.32,
          "startFrame": 16,
          "frames": 160
        },
        {
          "narration": "It walks the text one character at a time, no lookahead, no backtracking.",
          "lines": [
            3
          ],
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-2-step-1.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 4.76,
          "startFrame": 182,
          "frames": 143
        },
        {
          "narration": "An opening bracket simply deepens the nest: depth plus one, and on we go.",
          "lines": [
            4,
            5
          ],
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-2-step-2.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 5.8,
          "startFrame": 331,
          "frames": 174
        },
        {
          "narration": "A closing bracket climbs back out. If depth falls below zero, the closer arrived with nothing open, and the function quits immediately with false.",
          "lines": [
            6,
            7,
            8,
            9
          ],
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-2-step-3.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 8.52,
          "startFrame": 511,
          "frames": 256
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reaching the end is only half the story: the text is balanced exactly when depth comes back down to zero.",
          "lines": [
            10
          ],
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-2-step-4.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 6.6,
          "startFrame": 773,
          "frames": 198
