      "title": "Live trace: a) + b",
      "lang": "python",
      "code": "def is_balanced(text):\n    depth = 0\n    for ch in text:\n        if ch == '(':\n            depth += 1\n        elif ch == ')':\n            depth -= 1\n            if depth < 0:\n                return False\n    return depth == 0",
      "source": "snippets/is_balanced.py",
      "entry": "is_balanced",
      "args": "\"a) + b\"",
      "steps": [
        {
          "narration": "The input is the letter a, a closing parenthesis, then plus b. First the letter a arrives: neither branch matches, and depth stays at zero.",
          "toState": 5,
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-3-step-0.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 9.56,
          "startFrame": 16,
          "frames": 287
        },
        {
          "narration": "Then the closing parenthesis shows up. It is not an opener, so depth takes one step down and reads minus one.",
          "toState": 9,
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-3-step-1.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 6.28,
          "startFrame": 309,
          "frames": 189
        },
        {
          "narration": "The negative check fires before any other character is touched: the function returns false immediately, never looking at the rest of the text.",
          "toState": 11,
          "audioFile": "audio/scene-3-step-2.wav",
          "audioSeconds": 7.16,
